>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must be 3D or 4D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ ndim(v_1) ≤ 4
>>
Rule 2 (kernel size must be positive integer or tuple of two positive integers)
{v_1 : int ⊎ tuple(int)} |= v_1 > 0 ∧ v_1 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 3 (padding should be non-negative)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (stride must be positive)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 > 0
>>
Rule 6 (kernel size should not exceed padding)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int} |= v_1 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_1 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 8 (kernel size must be a tuple of two integers)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] > 0
>>
Rule 9 (stride must not be zero)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 10 (kernel size should be a single integer or tuple of two integers)
{v_1 : int ⊎ tuple(int)} |= v_1 ≠ 0 ∧ v_1 > 0
